course: dictionary
lesson: 10334
title: A trait is a feature
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A trait is a quality or feature that makes a person, animal or thing what it is. Some traits are about character, like being brave, shy or kind. «Mia always shares her crayons with new children» shows a kind trait.
explain: Traits can also be passed down from parents to children. Eye colour and the shape of a leaf are traits like this, and science calls them inherited traits. «Some people have a family trait, passed down from their parents, that gives very little armpit smell and dry, flaky earwax.» Here trait means a feature handed down through the family.
explain: In English, when you describe a character, back each trait with evidence from the text. Ask yourself: what does the character do or say that proves this trait? A good answer names the trait and points to a sentence that shows it.
fact: A trait is a quality or feature of a person, animal or thing.
fact: A character trait is a quality of someone's personality, such as being brave or shy.
fact: In science, a trait is passed down from parents to children, such as eye colour.
fact: Other phrases you may meet are «personality trait» and «family trait».
fact: «Trait» is a noun. One trait, two traits.
exercise: «Being brave and shy are both character traits.» What is a trait? | A loud noise | A type of weather | A place where people meet | *A quality or feature of someone's character
exercise: In science, what does a trait such as eye colour show? | *A feature passed down from parents to children | A kind of food that children like | A rule for playing a game | A feeling of being hungry
exercise: Which of these is a family trait? | A book about trains | A bus stop in the town centre | A sunny afternoon at the park | *Eye colour that children inherit from their parents
test: In an English lesson, what should you do when you name a character trait? | *Back it up with a sentence from the text that shows it | Copy the title of the book | Guess, and say the character is happy | Say the character is funny
test: Which word is the plural of trait? | traited | traitor | *traits | trait's
exam: «Some people have a family trait that gives very little armpit smell.» What does trait mean here? | A loud, rude word | A type of music | *A feature passed down from parents | A quick walk to the shop
